WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.890
<i>As long as good exists in this world,</i>

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.770
<b>Narrator</b>

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.770
<b>Hiroyuki Takano</b>

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>so, too, shall evil thrive.</i>

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.030
<i>But behind this eternal 
clash of good and evil,</i>

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.540
<i>there is another battle that goes unseen.</i>

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.810
What is... this power?!

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.500
<b>Magnetic Ore Monster
Adamant</b>

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.280
My magnetism produces a particular field!

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.870
Within that field, your Buster Blade 
is a useless lump of scrap iron!

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.810
Now you'll meet your end!

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.080
Die, Divine Swordsman Blader!

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.930
Blader Punch!

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.730
Oh? You failed, then?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.010
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.040
Blader's the Divine Swordsman, you see,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.360
so I never expected he'd drop 
his sword and just punch me.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.610
From a toy sales perspective, 
it just seemed so unreasonable.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.620
A truly pathetic excuse.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.020
Are you prepared for the consequences?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.550
<b>How I'll Do Better in the Future</b>

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.570
Go on... write!

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.380
<b>Reflections on Experience</b>

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.970
<b>Name</b>

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.630
What you learned from your experience, 
and how you'll do better in the future.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.640
<b>Pluripotent Cellular Executive
Immortal Camula</b>

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.680
Make every word count.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.240
Carelessness will not be tolerated!

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.030
<b>— Episode 4 —

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.530
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
Assistant: Touka Kuroitsu</b>

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.540
It'd be nice to be an executive, huh?

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.610
Executive?

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.360
Y'know, I've never met those guys.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.290
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
Doctor: Hajime Sadamaki</b>

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.290
<b>Secret Society Agastia Monster Development Department
New Assistant: Wolf Bete</b>

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.290
Kinda sounds like a pain in the ass, though.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.360
Being an evil executive does 
carry a lot of responsibility.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.570
It's a serious meritocracy there.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.380
There still aren't many 
female executives, either.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.560
It's such a dream job for me.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.240
Most of all because...

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:28.560
<b>Salary</b>

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.500
They command huge salaries!

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.920
Of course that's what you care about.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.560
That's a weirdly practical 
reason to have a dream.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.550
I get where you're coming from,

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:35.870
but we really need to think up a new monster 
idea for the upcoming battle with Blader.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.450
How'd they like the proposal I submitted?!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.440
<b>Protective scarf that
deflects all attacks</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.440
<b>Rips apart
 enemies with
 super-sharp
 claws!!!!</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.950
<b>Frickin' awesome gun
that shoots targets
30 light-years away!!</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.950
<b>Eternal Flare Cosmic
Dingo Monster Surrounded
 by Everlasting Flames</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:46.450
<b>Commands rad spiritual
 flames!!</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:46.450
<b>Mach-speed kicks</b>

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.950
My Eternal Flare Cosmic Dingo monster 
surrounded by everlasting flames?!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.460
You think they'd accept
 that pathetic scribble?!

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:51.320
Ideas aside, I'd really like to scale 
up our development capabilities.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.450
I've got lots of ideas that are impossible
 under our current technological restraints.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.720
Development capabilities, eh?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.600
That won't be easy.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.110
Maybe if we could get some 
new research material...

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.220
Hardly working, are we?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.640
These <i>are</i> business hours, are they not?

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.610
Yet you don't seem to be 
doing much business.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.980
<i>Agastia's Pluripotent Cellular Executive,</i>

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.430
<i>Immortal Camula.</i>

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.620
<i>She's a vampire monster whose entire body</i>

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.170
<i>is made up of special cells said 
to have universal application.</i>

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.240
<i>She demands strict adherence 
to rules and order,</i>

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.250
<i>and is spoken of in rumor as ruthlessly 
enforcing full-cellular commitment to work.</i>

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.010
L-Lady Camula!

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:41.500
It appears I will have to 
perform a personal audit.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.760
An executive audit?!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.010
What's the big deal with that, Miss Kuroitsu?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:51.450
Once, one of the combat-oriented executives 
dropped in for a surprise audit.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.520
<b>Force of Power Executive
Warrior of Jaguar</b>

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:04.030
<b>Spirit!</b>

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.230
He gave us this totally 
non-specific chewing out,

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.520
and all his suggestions were really generic, 
abstract philosophical principles.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.910
And when we submitted our report to him later,
 he'd completely forgotten all of it!

