00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.520
This hierarchy and top-down structure 
is how you ended up in a female body,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.540
and how Cannon ended up being a fluffy bird.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.680
Executive

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.680
Monster Development Department

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.950
Your work has been slowing down lately.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.600
It's been a while since you've had 
an equipment inspection, too.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.440
We don't want malfunctions 
occurring in crucial moments.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.660
I've gone through the check sheet,

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.430
but it might be best to have 
a specialist go over it again.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.530
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.200
<i>It's a proper audit.</i>

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.320
I'm curious.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.200
Why have your monster production 
costs been rising lately?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.680
That was my idea.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.640
I wanted our designs to have a 
little more... breathing room?

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.960
More shades of gray, I guess you'd say.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.110
Shades of gray?

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:03.920
Yes.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:08.720
Previous monsters were made unable to 
perform anything but their immediate function.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.560
I thought giving them a little 
more individuality and flexibility

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.710
would let them perform a variety of jobs.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:18.860
That's a big part of why Wolfie didn't have a 
complete breakdown despite his female body.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.180
I <i>did</i> have a complete breakdown!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.220
I'm totally getting this fixed, you got it?!

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:28.750
And why Cannon, who was created for long-range
 combat, can act as a mascot at events.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:28.750
Here you go! Have fun! Can I help you?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.070
So fluffy!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.740
I can't reach the balloon! Move it down!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.130
I see. Shades of gray...

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.060
<i>Performing outside their original function...</i>

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.750
<i>That could be a legitimate philosophy.</i>

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.490
I approve of your explanation of the costs,

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.690
but I can't overlook your 
dismal track record!

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:48.500
The fact remains that you've 
never once beaten Blader!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.840
You're absolutely right.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.640
There's nothing that can justify our failure.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.240
Lady Camula...

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.920
I'd like to make a request to you to 
improve our development capabilities.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.900
Tell me. I may consider it.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:07.620
Could I ask for some of your pluripotent 
cells to use as research material?

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.910
I'm positive that new materials will lead to 
new strides in monster development research!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:18.140
Oh? You're asking me to 
submit myself to testing?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.050
<i>She really is fearless when 
it comes to her objectives.</i>

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.790
Request denied.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.030
Agastia is not a school club.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.230
It's a meritocratic evil organization.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:33.350
If you need those cells, then take 
them by whatever means necessary.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:38.200
You're challenging me to 
shed your blood, then?

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.720
Precisely.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.480
Just what I was waiting for!

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.470
Wolfie boy!

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.310
Right!

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.850
Bete Claw!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.900
Wolf Bete.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.490
Modeled on the la Bête du Gévaudan 
of France, were you not?

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:06.740
This is that wolfman monster who 
was switched to a female form, yes?

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:08.660
Wolfie!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.320
I admire your spirit, but you've
 got a long way to go.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:20.180
Perhaps it's time I reminded 
you who's in charge here!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.290
No!

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.720
Please, no, Lady Camula!

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.550
Forgive him!

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:28.310
Are you talking back to me?!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.950
Lady Camula, this is going too far!

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.620
And one for you, too!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.310
Have I made myself clear?

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.980
See that you have results by 
the time of your next audit.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:54.450
Guess we won't be solving the development 
capability issue any time soon.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:55.840
What did you expect?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.480
It's not that easy to get 
new research materials.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.520
We'll just have to stick 
with the slow and steady.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.570
Is it that time already?

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:04.470
I'm going off to do some research.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:05.680
Research? For what?

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.950
My latest idea for monster development.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.080
It's the age...

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:13.500
of idols!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.220
Thank you, everyone!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.530
<i>Idols really are so charming.</i>

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.870
Thank you!

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.610
<i>An idol monster that can 
win over people's hearts</i>

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.390
Thank you!

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:33.760
<i>would let us use our existing technology 
while exploring new avenues of potential.</i>

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.440
Thank you!

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:37.450
Getting to stand on this stage and see 
all your smiling faces makes me so happy!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.270
<i>But I need a motif.</i>

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:40.620
<i>I won't be able to do a spec comparison 
graph like I do with combat-oriented monsters,</i>

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.810
It's almost like a dream!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:46.840
I feel like we're standing on top of a 
cloud, riding on waves of good feeling!

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.420
<i>so I'll need a strong elevator 
pitch to get them to—</i>

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.230
I'm sorry...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.230
Oh, no, totally my fault!

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.070
I was just so lost in thought.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.220
But it's not a dream, is it?

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.980
No, it's reality.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.330
<i>The idols' performance 
has moved her to tears?</i>

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:57.060
I used to think idols were special creatures

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:58.320
<i>Their power to touch people's 
hearts really is something.</i>

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:02.500
who lived in different worlds 
than an ordinary girl like me.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.080
L-Lady Camula?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.810
But now that we're here, 
it's the same as it always was.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.730
What are you doing here?!

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:11.240
You've got the wrong person!

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.760
You're not convincing anyone like that!

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.590
Really, you don't have to run away.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.950
Lady Camula... you like idols?

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.570
Certainly not!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.450
Now for our next song!

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.670
This song was all we had back in 
our early days after our debut.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.550
It really means a lot to us!

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:35.020
Back then, the idea of singing in front of 
this many people really was like a dream.

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.280
For the miracle that brought us here...

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.020
...and for those of you who 
backed us all the way...

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:43.370
Please listen... to "Kimidrome"!

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.500
Sublime...

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.890
That good?!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.900
I've been buying their merchandise 
since their debut,

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.240
but it was my first time 
at one of their concerts.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.290
I refrained at first, 
because it seemed inappropriate

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.800
for an evil organization's executive 
to lose her mind at an idol concert.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.970
But when you started talking about
 making more versatile monsters,

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.880
I thought I'd come and see if it felt right.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.320
Honestly, there's nothing wrong with that.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.610
Even monsters need to live their lives.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:30.060
Seeing them live for the first time,

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.860
and thinking about all they've been through,

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:33.890
I just...

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.610
Forgive me for losing 
my composure, Kuroitsu.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.600
Really, it's no problem at all.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.780
I don't know a lot about idols, 
so I hope you'll teach me all about them.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.110
Really?!

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:05.540
No problem! I have all their albums, 
including first and alternate editions!

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.120
I've got DVDs, Blu-rays, and even UHDs!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.060
<i>Like a young enthusiast first 
meeting a kindred spirit...</i>

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:16.330
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell 
the others in the organization.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.580
Of course I won't.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.500
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.140
This is such a big help, Miss Kuroitsu!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:38.220
How'd you get those pluripotent cells?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.060
I promised never to tell.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.540
